#!/bin/zsh
# Mathis, 2026-10-15: "zoom out the current Codex painted world, the Sanctuary, with the Flame, so that it feels part of
# a larger world". Codex owns this (visual integration, no design by Claude). Builds on the surround Codex painted for
# the look-around (docs/design/flame-depth/sanctuary-surround.md). Re-run safe: skipped once the report exists.
ROOT="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)"; cd "$ROOT"
CODEX="/Applications/ChatGPT.app/Contents/Resources/codex-cli/bin/codex"
DONE=docs/plan-2.0/p32-sanctuary-zoom.md
[[ -f $DONE ]] && { echo "exists: $DONE"; exit 0; }
"$CODEX" exec -s workspace-write -C "$ROOT" -- "In the Swift app prototypes/p2-spikes/SpikeLab (the Hush game), zoom the Sanctuary (home, S2View.swift, your composed stage of decisions 170 and the look-around surround of docs/design/flame-depth/sanctuary-surround.md) OUT, so the Flame and its stone circle feel like part of a larger world (Mathis: 'zoom out the current painted world with the Flame so that it feels part of a larger world'). Show noticeably more of the surroundings around the circle (more ruins, waterfalls, sky, sea, paths), with the Flame smaller in proportion but still clearly the hero, still standing on its circle's centre, still sitting in the middle of the free space between the top panel and the quest panel (the app measures that space: model.feetTarget). Use and, if needed, extend the painted surround (outpaint more of the same scene, same style and palette; register it against the original as you did before) so that at rest AND at the look-around limits no edge, border or black stripe ever shows (decision 164). Keep the look-around working (same feel), the Flame's light pool and ground anchor, day/night, and the 60 fps rule (decision 165: no blurred .shadow over the world). Do not change the quest panel, Shell/HomeView.swift gestures, the other realms, or the map. Verify: build for the iOS simulator (xcodebuild -scheme SpikeLab from prototypes/p2-spikes), launch with -skipintro (and -push left / -push right for the limits; do NOT use -worldonly, it disables the Flame's placement), take screenshots before/after, check the edges. Write a short report to $DONE (what you changed, before/after screenshot paths under docs/design/flame-depth/verification/sanctuary-zoom/). Do not commit." < /dev/null > docs/reviews/p32-sanctuary-zoom.log 2>&1
[[ -f $DONE ]] && echo "done: $DONE" || echo "MISSING: $DONE (see docs/reviews/p32-sanctuary-zoom.log)"
